          "provider": "fal",
          "model": "seedance-2.0",
          "prompt": "Live-action footage, not animation. The reference video is a rough untextured 3D previz — take only its camera path, framing, and the three cut points; replace every surface with photoreal live action. A working lighthouse on a rocky point at blue hour: black weathered granite streaked with surging white surf, a steel-hulled fishing boat trailing a churned wake, peeling white paint on the stone tower, the lamp a soft volumetric shaft sweeping through sea mist — never a hard-edged cone. Shot 1: slow push-in across open water toward the point. Shot 2: low water-level chase behind the boat, spray flecking the lens. Shot 3: from the lantern-room gallery looking down as the boat crosses the beam, dark sea textured with moonlit swell. Full-frame cinema camera, 32mm anamorphic, shallow depth of field, gentle handheld drift, fine film grain; deep blue-hour palette, last ember of sunset on the horizon.",
